From de9d045a965d1a2bc4aca030dcf071d5ff33ebb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Curtin <ericcurtin17@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:37:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] asahi/hk: use a lighter CDM barrier between compute
 dispatches

agx_cdm_barrier() sets every known bit. Its comment says the extra bits
went in for blit cache coherency, that their meaning was not known, and
that it should be revisited. Add agx_cdm_barrier_light(), setting only
the bits that were set before that, and use it for CDM cache flushes.

Per-dispatch cost, M1 (G13G, 8 core), test-backend-ops perf -o ADD,
ne=[4096,1,1,1], 3 runs:

  agx_cdm_barrier()         7.1 - 7.4 us
  agx_cdm_barrier_light()   4.0 - 4.1 us

dEQP-VK, one build with only this behaviour toggled, baseline and
patched identical in every group including not-supported counts:

  synchronization, memory_model, compute.pipeline   13658 pass  0 fail
  image, blit, copy, texture                         2588 pass  0 fail
  draw, tessellation, geometry                       2611 pass  1 fail

The one failure is geometry.builtin_variable.primitive_id.matching,
which fails the same way with the old barrier.

The last group matters because hk_cmd_draw.c launches the vertex,
geometry and tessellation shaders through hk_dispatch_with_usc(), so
this changes the barrier after every draw, not just every dispatch. The
middle group includes blit_image generate_mipmaps, which chains
dependent blits, so it covers what the extra bits were added for.

This is not proof the dropped bits are unnecessary. unk_0..unk_19 are
undocumented, so all this shows is that nothing I can run notices.

Each remaining bit was checked by clearing it and re-running:

  unk_5 unk_6 unk_8   us    memory_model failures
    1     1     1     4.10        0
    1     1     0     1.61     1060 (+ 78/78 image.load_store)
    1     0     1     3.85       30
    0     1     1     3.96        0

So unk_8 and unk_6 are both load-bearing, and clearing them is caught.
That is also a positive control for the numbers above: the suite does
detect missing CDM cache maintenance, and it is silent on this patch.
Clearing unk_6 only fails 30 of 17300, so a smaller run would have
missed it.

unk_5 looks droppable and saves 3.4%, but on undocumented bits with a
failure rate that low I would rather keep it.
---
 src/asahi/libagx/libagx_dgc.h      | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 src/asahi/vulkan/hk_cmd_dispatch.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/asahi/libagx/libagx_dgc.h b/src/asahi/libagx/libagx_dgc.h
index d8266b663111..61309e181ee1 100644
--- a/src/asahi/libagx/libagx_dgc.h
+++ b/src/asahi/libagx/libagx_dgc.h
@@ -415,6 +415,23 @@ agx_cdm_barrier(GLOBAL uint32_t *out, enum agx_chip chip)
    return out;
 }
 
+/* Only the bits agx_cdm_barrier() set before the blit fixes added the rest. */
+static inline GLOBAL uint32_t *
+agx_cdm_barrier_light(GLOBAL uint32_t *out, enum agx_chip chip)
+{
+   agx_push(out, CDM_BARRIER, cfg) {
+      cfg.unk_5 = true;
+      cfg.unk_6 = true;
+      cfg.unk_8 = true;
+
+      if (chip == AGX_CHIP_G13X) {
+         cfg.unk_4 = true;
+      }
+   }
+
+   return out;
+}
+
 static inline GLOBAL uint32_t *
 agx_vdm_return(GLOBAL uint32_t *out)
 {
diff --git a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_cmd_dispatch.c b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_cmd_dispatch.c
index 7cb08bb1d3c8..6aa66ce59cc0 100644
--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_cmd_dispatch.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_cmd_dispatch.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ hk_cdm_cache_flush(struct hk_device *dev, struct hk_cs *cs)
    assert(cs->current + AGX_CDM_BARRIER_LENGTH < cs->end &&
           "caller must ensure space");
 
-   cs->current = agx_cdm_barrier(cs->current, dev->dev.chip);
+   cs->current = agx_cdm_barrier_light(cs->current, dev->dev.chip);
    cs->stats.flushes++;
 }
 
